                <pb facs="0150" n="142" sameAs="frus:frus1941v03/pg142"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">561.321D1 Advisory Committee/64: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Caffery</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-10-23T19:00:00-05:00">October 23, 1941—7
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1000. In view of decrease in price of Brazilian cotton the subsidy on exports of
                    United States cotton to Canada has been increased to 3 cents in accordance with
                    the plan referred to in last sentence of Section C, our telegram no. 804 of
                    September 15, 1941.</p>
                <p>Repeat to São Paulo.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
